:: MMA Gym Avery First Response
<<effects>>
<<if $mmaGymAWChoice is "form">>
    Avery closes the distance between you, walking with the confidence of someone who fully expects other people to get out of <<his>> way.
    <br><br>
    "Your shoulders are a mess," <<he>> says, not bothering with a greeting. "You're just wasting energy."
    <br><br>
    <<He>> gestures toward an empty bench, then criticizes your stance with a disappointed click of <<his>> tongue. "Again. Slower. Form first, speed later."
    <br><br>
    You try to adjust your posture. Avery is already correcting your grip before you even finish the rep.<<gtiredness>><<gstress>><<stress 4>><<tiredness 10>>
    <br><br>
    "And don't pout," <<he>> adds smoothly. "Pouting is not a muscle group."<<npcincr Avery dom 1>><<gdom>><<pass 10>>
<<elseif $mmaGymAWChoice is "status">>
    Avery glances around the room, as if just now remembering that the general public is, in fact, allowed in here.
    <br><br>
    "The equipment is passable. The ventilation is decent," <<he>> says, draping the towel around <<his>> neck. "The lack of privacy, however, is tragic."
    <br><br>
    Right on cue, someone a few feet away drops a heavy barbell with a loud metallic crash, followed by an aggressive grunt.
    <br><br>
    Avery doesn't flinch, but <<his>> expression turns incredibly sour.
    "Case in point," <<he>> sighs. "The best machines are completely wasted on people who mistake loud suffering for discipline."<<pass 5>>
<<elseif $mmaGymAWChoice is "watch">>
    Avery catches you staring. Instead of looking away, <<he>> holds your gaze in the mirror, stepping right back onto the treadmill and immediately bumping the incline up two levels.
    <br><br>
    "Keep your eyes away," <<he>> says, watching your reflection. "If you stare that openly, I might think you're actually impressed."
    <br><br>
    The treadmill speeds up to a grueling pace. You wait for <<him>> to break form, but <<he>> refuses to give you the satisfaction.
	The only signs of strain are the tight grip <<his>> knuckles have on the rail, the flush creeping up <<his>> neck, and a thin, dark line of sweat finally bleeding through the back of <<his>> shirt.
    <br><br>
    "Cardio isn't the hard part," Avery says, voice impressively steady over the noise of the belt. "Keeping your standards high when you're exhausted... that's where most people embarrass themselves."<<pass 5>>
<<else>>
    "To train," Avery repeats. The look <<he>> gives you lands somewhere between skeptical and amused.
    <br><br>
    "See that you actually do. Drifting aimlessly between machines until you feel a vague sense of accomplishment doesn't count."
    Avery taps <<his>> treadmill display. The screen shows a custom interval routine programmed with heart-rate targets and rest periods. It looks like a punishing financial spreadsheet.
    <br><br>
    "Structure prevents excuses," <<he>> says, hitting a button to save the data. "You should try it sometime."<<npcincr Avery love 1>><<stress -3>><<pass 10>><<glove>><<lstress>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|MMA Gym Avery First Offer]]>><</link>>


:: MMA Gym Avery First Offer
<<effects>>
Avery steps off the treadmill with efficiency. <<He>> folds <<his>> towel, checks <<his>> watch, and turns to you,
looking like <<hes>> already bored.
"Your gear is a disaster. Your form is worse. I've seen better training in a daycare."
<br><br>
Before you can decide if <<hes>> insulting you or just stating a fact, <<he>> continues.
<br><br>
"There's a premium tier here. Private lockers, decent showers, and fewer people... I could get you access.
It would be significantly less painful than watching you improvise for another month."
<br><br>
It's phrased as a generous offer, but it lands like a direct command.
<br><br>
"For now," <<he>> says, already walking toward the exit, "you're joining me for a smoothie in the lounge. It's organic,
absurdly expensive, and marginally tolerable if you order the right one."
<br><br>
Avery doesn't wait for your answer. <<Hes>> already headed for the lounge.
<br><br>
<<link [[Join Avery in the lounge (0:20)|MMA Gym Avery First End]]>><<set $mmaGymAWChoice2 to "accept">><<pass 20>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Say you don't need Avery's money (0:05)|MMA Gym Avery First End]]>><<set $mmaGymAWChoice2 to "refuse">><<pass 5>><</link>>


